  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 810031e0539baf849a8ec048a6ff4b7a, type: 3}
  m_Name: help_food
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Antarium.Content::Antarium.Content.HelpTopicDef
  id: help_food
  displayName: Food
  order: 160
  category: Basics
  icon: food
  body: 'Every ant eats, and the queen most of all. Food in the top bar shows what you have, how much fits, and what you gain or lose per minute.


    Food comes from:

    - seeds, berries, apples and toadstools on the surface, which workers forage by themselves (seeds, berries and apples only by day);

    - grub nests in the topsoil: pale speckled soil that drops grubs when it is dug;

    - mushrooms in caves, which grow back after they are picked;

    - the Fungus Garden (research Fungiculture), which turns seeds or leaves into much more food.


    When food runs out the colony starves: everyone works at half speed and the queen stops laying. No ant starves to death, and it ends as soon as food comes in.'
  reveal: 0
  revealBiome: {fileID: 0}
  revealResearch: {fileID: 0}
